meta {
  name: Read one of my wishlist entries
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}{{apiPrefix}}/me/wishlist/{{wishlistItemId}}
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

docs {
  The owner's view of one wishlist entry. Identical to a row from the public
  `GET /users/{username}/wishlist` except that it also carries `notes`, which
  the public read deliberately omits: notes are the one per-user wishlist field
  nobody but their author should see, so they are only served to a request that
  proved whose they are.

  This is what the owner's edit form calls before it can show the notes field.

  - 200 the entry, with notes
  - 404 nonexistent or someone else's
}
